# 深い入れ子の文章 (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py: the desktop's own text editor (open,
# docproc kernel) and the text editor running as a process (pdoc) open the same text, whose
# elements are nested as deep as a record may be (32: tad, document, p and 29 font), with an
# opened link to the text itself, so that what is inside the link is drawn again inside it
# as deep as an opened link is drawn on the screen (TV_MAX_DEPTH). The window is shot in both
# and compared inside it (101,125 to 682,482 of the screen), a letter typed into the deepest
# run and saved: record 0 the same, byte for byte, but for the identity of each copy, which its
# link to itself names (sum anon). The process says how much of its main
# task's stack it used ("document: stack used N of 65536 bytes"); the desktop's stack is said
# by stkuse. Nothing falls: no exception, no stack run over. The shots on opening (deep_*_open)
# are the same, and so are those after the letter is typed (deep_*_typed): both draw the
# object inside its links to itself as it is being edited (the process by tv_src_live).
# Keys: x 1b; End 4D; Ctrl+S 16 01, Ctrl+E 08 01.
docproc kernel
# the deepest there may be
mkbig doc 1
xml <tad version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"><document>
xml <p>深い入れ子の文章</p>
xml <p>
xml <font color="#000000">
